<%# locals: () %>
<%# The "···" of the meetings heads ("Alle Meetings" and a project's meetings),
    beside the "?". It holds the way into the glossary (user, 04.11.2026):
    the glossary serves the transcription of meetings, so it is reached from
    here, not from the sidebar. Only for those who may read it
    (GlossaryPolicy); without it the menu renders nothing.
    A menu item, not a word in the head (user, 2026-11-10): the heads of the
    application hold the page's action, "···" and "?", and a cobalt link
    there was the one of its kind. The inbox keeps its other pages
    (exceptions, settings) behind its "···" the same way.
    _top: the heads stand beside frames, and the glossary is a page of its own. %>
<%= render Neo::OverflowMenuComponent.new do |menu| %>
  <% if policy(GlossaryTerm).index? %>
    <% menu.with_item(label: t('navigation.glossary'), url: organisation_glossary_terms_path(@current_organisation),
                      icon: 'book', data: { turbo_frame: '_top', meetings_glossary_link: true }) %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
